$NetBSD$

Fix the path of OpenBSD's wsconsctl.conf.

The entry has read /etc/wsconsctlctl.conf since it was added upstream in
aa3bc264 (2013), so it has never matched anything.  The file OpenBSD's
/etc/rc actually applies is /etc/wsconsctl.conf, one wsconsctl(8) variable
assignment per line:

	keyboard.encoding=ru
	display.screen_off=60000

Rx.word already allows the dots in those keys, so Simplevars parses the file
as it stands.  NetBSD is unaffected: it has /etc/wscons.conf, which is a
different file in a different format.

Going upstream as well; the branch is wsconsctl-conf-typo in
zakinko/augeas.  This header gets the PR number once it is open.

--- lenses/simplevars.aug.orig
+++ lenses/simplevars.aug
@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@
            . incl "/etc/audit/auditd.conf"
            . incl "/etc/adduser.conf"
            . incl "/etc/mixerctl.conf"
-           . incl "/etc/wsconsctlctl.conf"
+           . incl "/etc/wsconsctl.conf"
            . incl "/etc/ocsinventory/ocsinventory-agent.cfg"
 
 let xfm = transform lns filter
